╰┈➤Searching Pattern 3 — Binary Search
#Linear Search Works on: [10, 5, 20, 8, 15]
We can check: 10 -> 5 -> 20 -> 8 -> 15 every element -> Time: O(n)

#Binary Search - Requires a sorted collection
arr = [2, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30]  -> Instead of checking every element- we repeatedly cut the search space in half ->That's the entire idea anthee

##╰┈➤The Core Idea chudhaama (start -> middle -> compare)
arr = [2, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30]
target = 25

#Start:
left                    right
 |                        |
[2, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30]

#Find the middle:
middle = (left + right) // 2 #10

#Compare: 10 < 25

-> Because the array is sorted, we immediately know: Everything to the left of 10 is also too small
So discard half: [10, 15, 20, 25, 30]
                  |                |
                left            right

#Again find middle: 20 and Compare: 20 < 25 ->Discard everything before it
-> Now: [25, 30] and Middle: 25 ->Found kadaa

╰┈➤Ikkada The Three Decisions anthee
Every iteration asks exactly one question: arr[mid] == target
If yes: FOUND

If: arr[mid] < target  ->Target must be on the right: left = mid + 1
If: arr[mid] > target  ->Target must be on the left: right = mid - 1 ##Antee idee binary search

╰┈➤Basic code ownga try cheyandii
arr = [2, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30]
target = 25

left = 0
right = len(arr) - 1

while left <= right:
    mid = (left + right) // 2
    if arr[mid] == target:
        print("Found")
        break
    elif arr[mid] < target:
        left = mid + 1
    else:
        right = mid - 1 # Found

╰┈➤Enduku Binary Search usefuland powerful avuthundi
Linear Search  -> O(n)
Binary Search  -> O(log n) #Ee log n pattern is one of the most important concepts in DS gurthupetkondii

Suppose you have: 1,000 elements -> Linear search may require around: 1,000 comparisons
                                 -> Binary search: 1000 -> 500 ->250 -> 125 -> 62 -> 31 -> 15 -> 7 -> 3 -> 1 #Only around 10 iterations
For: 1,000,000 elements -> Binary search needs roughly: 20 iterations because: 2²⁰ ≈ 1,000,000 antheena??

ikkada Binary search is not: A faster version of linear search
-> A search strategy that exploits sorted order to eliminate half of the remaining possibilities at every step

